-- CISSP Domain 5 expansion, part A: objective 5.1 (control access to assets - least privilege/need-to-know applied via ACLs vs capability lists, RuBAC, constrained user interfaces, content/context-dependent control, centralized vs decentralized administration, default deny, dual control, privileged access management; IAAA basics and DAC/MAC/RBAC/ABAC definitions intentionally NOT restated, see ci-f-039/040/041/044/045/100/101 and ci-a-010..013), 5.2 (identity & authentication mgmt - biometric modalities/liveness detection, HOTP/TOTP, push-bombing/MFA fatigue, password spraying, rainbow tables, FIDO2/WebAuthn, adaptive authentication; MFA factor categories, FAR/FRR/CER, pass-the-hash, and credential stuffing intentionally NOT restated, see ci-f-040/042/104/106/107 and ci-q-115/116), and 5.3 (integrate identity as a third-party service - federated identity management, circle of trust, cloud identity providers, on-prem/cloud/hybrid identity architecture, directory sync, SCIM, identity brokers, JIT provisioning, B2B/B2C federation; SAML/OAuth/OIDC basics intentionally NOT restated, see ci-f-102 and ci-q-110/111).


